WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.919
Marilla's newly adopted twins, Davy and Dora, were not noticeably alike, although both were fair.

2
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.597
Dora had long curls that always looked perfect.

3
00:00:11.598 --> 00:00:16.593
Davy had a crop of fuzzy little yellow ringlets all over his round head.

4
00:00:16.594 --> 00:00:22.712
Dora's hazel eyes were gentle and mild. Davy's eyes were mischievous.

5
00:00:22.713 --> 00:00:29.496
After the twins had arrived at Green Gables and unpacked, they had their first dinner with their new family.

6
00:00:29.497 --> 00:00:36.640
At the dinner table, Dora behaved like a little lady, but Davy's manners left much to be desired.

7
00:00:36.641 --> 00:00:43.126
"I'm so hungry I don't have time to eat politely," he said when Marilla scolded him.

8
00:00:43.127 --> 00:00:47.382
"That cake's really delicious," Davy said.

9
00:00:47.383 --> 00:00:54.637
"We haven't eaten cake for so long because mother was too sick to make it. Can I have another piece?"

10
00:00:54.638 --> 00:00:59.999
Marilla would have refused, but Anne cut a generous second slice.

11
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.596
As she passed it to Davy, she reminded him that he should say thank you.

12
00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:08.492
Davy merely grinned at Anne and took a huge bite.

13
00:01:08.493 --> 00:01:15.190
When Davy had finished the slice he said, "If you'll give me another piece, I'll say thank you."

14
00:01:15.191 --> 00:01:21.169
"No, you've had plenty of cake," said Marilla in a stern tone.

15
00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:28.907
Davy winked at Anne and then snatched Dora's first piece of cake, from which she had taken only one dainty little bite.

16
00:01:28.908 --> 00:01:33.142
He opened his mouth wide and crammed the whole slice in.

17
00:01:33.143 --> 00:01:37.320
Dora's lip trembled, and Marilla was speechless with anger.

18
00:01:37.321 --> 00:01:45.742
Anne promptly exclaimed, in her best schoolteacher's voice, "Davy, gentlemen don't do things like that."

19
00:01:45.743 --> 00:01:52.823
"I know they don't," said Davy, as soon as he could speak. "But I'm not a gentleman."

20
00:01:52.824 --> 00:01:56.748
"Don't you want to be?" said Anne.

21
00:01:56.749 --> 00:02:03.406
"Of course I do," said Davy. "But you can't be a gentleman till you grow up."

22
00:02:03.407 --> 00:02:07.811
"You can start to be a gentleman now , Davy," Anne

23
00:02:07.812 --> 00:02:13.214
said. "And gentlemen never snatch things or forget to say thank

24
00:02:13.215 --> 00:02:16.460
you." "Gentlemen don't have much fun," said

25
00:02:16.461 --> 00:02:19.654
Davy. "I think I'll wait till I'm grown

26
00:02:19.655 --> 00:02:28.544
up." "Davy and Dora, it's time for bed," said Marilla, who was exhausted and wondering how she would ever cope with

27
00:02:28.545 --> 00:02:33.242
Davy. Marilla would remember the first week with the twins

28
00:02:33.243 --> 00:02:39.874
forever. It wasn't so different from the second week or the third week, but by the third week she was used to life with

29
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:45.697
them. It seemed that Davy was always causing mischief or devising

30
00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:51.132
it. Davy's first major exploit occurred two days after his arrival, on Sunday

31
00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:54.882
morning. Anne dressed him for church while Marilla looked after

32
00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:58.842
Dora. Davy objected strongly to having his face

33
00:02:58.843 --> 00:03:05.891
washed. "Marilla washed it yesterday, and that's enough for one week. It's more comfortable being

34
00:03:05.892 --> 00:03:11.848
dirty." "Paul Irving washes his face every day by himself," said

35
00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:15.967
Anne. Davy had been living at Green Gables for little over 48 hours,

36
00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:21.921
but he already worshipped Anne and hated Paul Irving, even though he hadn't met him yet.

37
00:03:21.922 --> 00:03:26.826
Anne had praised Paul enthusiastically the day after Davy's arrival.

38
00:03:26.827 --> 00:03:31.351
If Paul Irving washed his face every day, that settled it.

39
00:03:31.352 --> 00:03:34.984
He, Davy Keith, would do it too.

40
00:03:34.985 --> 00:03:38.910
At church Davy behaved quite well at first.

41
00:03:38.911 --> 00:03:42.773
He looked at all the boys and wondered which one was Paul Irving.

42
00:03:42.774 --> 00:03:46.810
But then Davy looked at the girl sitting in front of him.

43
00:03:46.811 --> 00:03:50.468
She was dressed in a violet dress with a frilly neck.

44
00:03:50.469 --> 00:03:56.822
Davy thrust his hand into his pocket and produced a furry, squirming caterpillar.

45
00:03:56.823 --> 00:04:01.087
Marilla saw Davy and tried to grab him, but she was too late.

46
00:04:01.088 --> 00:04:04.918
Davy dropped the caterpillar down the girl's neck.

47
00:04:04.919 --> 00:04:10.393
In the middle of the minister's prayer, there was a series of piercing shrieks.

48
00:04:10.394 --> 00:04:15.539
The minister stopped and opened his eyes. Every head turned.

49
00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:22.715
Laura White was dancing up and down on the church pew, clutching frantically at the back of her dress.

50
00:04:22.716 --> 00:04:33.282
"Oh, Mommy, Mommy! Eek! Get it out! That bad boy put it down my neck! Mommy, it's going further down. Ahh!"

51
00:04:33.283 --> 00:04:38.301
Mrs. White rose and carried the hysterical Laura out of church.

52
00:04:38.302 --> 00:04:45.435
Marilla and Anne held Davy firmly for the rest of the church service, and their faces stayed a bright red.

53
00:04:45.436 --> 00:04:51.705
When they got home, Marilla put Davy to bed and made him stay there for the rest of the day.

54
00:04:51.706 --> 00:04:54.857
Later Anne went into his room.

55
00:04:54.858 --> 00:05:03.994
"I suppose," Davy said, "that Paul Irving wouldn't have dropped a caterpillar down a girl's neck in church, would he?"

56
00:05:03.995 --> 00:05:08.668
"Indeed he wouldn't," said Anne sadly.

57
00:05:08.669 --> 00:05:12.439
"Well, I'm kind of sorry I did it then," said Davy.

58
00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:17.767
"But it was such a big caterpillar. It seemed a pity to waste him.

59
00:05:17.768 --> 00:05:23.962
And say, wasn't it fun to hear that girl yell?" Anne looked sternly at Davy.

60
00:05:23.963 --> 00:05:31.064
"I . . . did something else today," Davy went on in a muffled voice.

61
00:05:31.065 --> 00:05:36.305
"I'm sorry now, but I'm awful scared to tell you."

62
00:05:36.306 --> 00:05:41.027
"Davy, what is it you've done?" Anne asked.

63
00:05:41.028 --> 00:05:46.665
"I put a toad in Marilla's bed. You can go and take it out if you like.

64
00:05:46.666 --> 00:05:51.629
But say, Anne, wouldn't it be fun to leave it there?"

65
00:05:51.630 --> 00:06:01.612
"Davy Keith!" Anne sprang from Davy's clinging arms and ran across the hall to Marilla's room. The bed was slightly rumpled.

66
00:06:01.613 --> 00:06:08.064
Anne nervously drew back the blankets and there was the toad, blinking at her from under a pillow.

67
00:06:08.065 --> 00:06:15.733
"How can I carry that awful thing out?" moaned Anne with a shudder, and then she got a shovel from the yard.

68
00:06:15.734 --> 00:06:26.819
"With Davy at home and Anthony Pye at school, my nerves are almost worn out!" thought Anne.

